    "verdict": "THRESHOLD/CALIBRATION IS THE PROBLEM. The frozen threshold 0.5523 is grossly mismatched to the test prob distribution (mean 0.39, mass piled at 0/1; model is OVER-confident, ECE 0.138). The test-label ceiling is only 0.866 above the frozen 0.831 (gap 0.035), and a fair VAL-derived threshold applied BLIND to test recovers +0.034 (96% of the gap) -> 0.865, within noise of the ceiling. So essentially the ENTIRE 0.831->0.866 gap is honestly recoverable by thresholding/calibration. The AUC=0.932 ceiling only bites ABOVE ~0.866 \u2014 that residual is model-limited and NOT recoverable without a better model."
